                <pb facs="0258" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg174"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Received 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>August 6, 10 a.m. Confidential. Note reference to treaty 1846 in the committee
                    report. Colombia dreads above all things newspaper reported intention of the
                    United States to denounce the treaty in the event of rejecting canal treaty.</p>
                <p>I have additional confirmation the statement of my dispatch No. 49 June 15.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
